The copy is performed by `scripts/vendor-cma.sh` (re-runnable, reads a local clone
of upstream from a gitignored `.vendor-src/`), followed by
`scripts/localize-fixtures.py`. This file records what came from upstream and, per
Apache License 2.0 §4(b), which of those files carry modifications.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Vendored destinations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream source is copied into THREE places, because each agent package must be
independently deployable (the sandbox only has that one package's own tree) and the
web app needs the same fixtures:

  A. agenthub/agents/cma-shopping/runtime/src/
       commerce-common/          <- commerce-common/
       shopping-agent-core/      <- shopping-agent/core/
       storefront-stdio-server/  <- NEW code (this repo), which vendors a slice of
                                    upstream examples/ as package data under
                                    storefront_stdio_server/_examples/

  B. agenthub/agents/cma-merchant/runtime/src/
       commerce-common/          <- commerce-common/          (second copy)
       shopping-agent-core/      <- shopping-agent/core/      (second copy;
                                    MockRetailMerchant wraps a MockRetail instance)
       merchant-agent-core/      <- merchant-agent/core/
       merchant-stdio-server/    <- NEW code (this repo), which vendors a slice of
                                    upstream examples/ as package data under
                                    merchant_stdio_server/_examples/

  C. apps/storefront-web/data/retail/
       catalog.json, orders.json, policies.json, users.json  <- examples/retail/data/

Not vendored anywhere: runtime-agent-sdk, runtime-messages-api, the example FastAPI
hosts, and the parts of examples/ none of the above needs.

