--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Modified files (Apache License 2.0 §4(b))
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3.1 Carried presentation chips — agenthub/agents/cma-shopping/runtime/src/

  commerce-common/commerce_common/presentation.py
  commerce-common/commerce_common/turn.py
  shopping-agent-core/shopping_agent/tools/registry.py

  A turn's suggestion chips ride along on the turn's last presentation component
  (a shared `suggestions` field, lifted into a second `ui` event) instead of
  costing a model round of their own. This saves one round trip per turn on a
  latency-sensitive demo. cma-merchant's copies of the same two packages are NOT
  modified.

3.2 Package-data stubs — both stdio-server packages

  _examples/demo_common/__init__.py
  _examples/retail/__init__.py

  Both REPLACED with empty stubs. Upstream's real `__init__.py` re-exports modules
  that pull in the CMA example FastAPI host and the merchant runtime; neither is
  needed to run `MockRetail`, and importing them would make these packages depend
  on trees this repo deliberately does not vendor. This is the one packaging
  exception that lets `mock_retail.py` and `storefront_fixtures.py` stay unedited.

3.3 Localized fixtures — all three destinations (A, B and C above)

  retail/data/*.json

  Rewritten by `scripts/localize-fixtures.py` after every vendor run: amounts
  converted to CNY, a language preference added to demo-user. The script is
  idempotent (it recognizes a `_localized` marker), so re-running vendor + localize
  does not double-convert. Do not hand-edit these files — the next vendor run
  overwrites them.

  Upstream fixtures NOT copied: memory-seed.json everywhere, and the merchant_*.json
  files in destinations A and C (shopping-only scope there).

3.4 Skills — 10 files

  agenthub/agents/cma-shopping/.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md   (5, from shopping-agent/skills/)
  agenthub/agents/cma-merchant/.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md   (5, from merchant-agent/skills/)

  Light edits: tool-name annotations, `web_search` references removed. Each file's
  own header records what changed.

3.5 Derived system prompts

  agenthub/agents/cma-shopping/CLAUDE.md
  agenthub/agents/cma-merchant/CLAUDE.md

  Derived from upstream's managed-agent `system.md`. The derivation is re-runnable
  and its steps are recorded in each package's
  `runtime/scripts/derive-claude-md.{md,py}`; upstream's original is committed
  alongside under `runtime/scripts/_vendor-reference/`.

